      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine, a key amino acid, acts as a major signaling molecule to switch on the mTOR pathway, which is the central regulator for muscle protein synthesis. It's like a master switch that tells the muscle cells, \"Time to build!\" A caloric surplus provides the necessary raw materials, or energy, for the body to perform this intense building process. This surplus ensures that the body has enough energy to process the nitrogen from the amino acids into new muscle tissue, thereby positively impacting nitrogen balance.",
